      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was laid out in 1849 and officially incorporated in 1881, marking its formal emergence in Iowa history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chillicothe%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first school in Chillicothe was a one‑room building called Chillicothe #1, which was later demolished and no longer stands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chillicothe%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Chillicothe is the burial site of Curtis King, the oldest living Civil War veteran at the time of his death.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chillicothe%2C_Iowa",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The city sits within Wapello County, Iowa, and is known for its quiet, historically rich atmosphere.",
